(Thus overall plan steps:)
(1. Prepare origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha (candidate_prepared).)
(2. Assign operator to origin, activate node, lock availability (which also confirms), release operator.)
(3. Assign operator to destination, activate node, lock availability, release operator.)
(4. Prepare shift_candidate_beta (candidate_prepared).)
(5. Allocate vehicle_unit_beta to destination_availability_alpha (link and allocate).)
(6. Load cargo onto origin and destination nodes.)
(7. Assemble transport leg (need origin and destination availability locked, nodes ready, etc). We'll need to assemble the leg after locking and confirming availabilities.)
(8. Authorize transport leg loading.)
(9. Load container onto leg? Actually we need loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha and loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta. So we need to load container beta onto leg. For that we need loading_container_beta available, candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta (we have), candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha (already), candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta (already), loading_container_available loading_container_beta (yes), transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not loading_container_loaded. So we need to assemble leg, authorize loading, then load container.)
